WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.600
Speaker 1: Let's jump right in, because there's
so much to discuss today, I believe it was

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:09.430
two weeks ago, we did a live stream covering
this horrible mass shooting that took place

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:11.410
in San Jose.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:16.240
And I was saying and many people in the audience
were saying, as we were watching the press

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:21.210
conferences and the calls for thoughts and
prayers and support of the families and all

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:25.900
of this stuff, are we ever going to do anything
or are we even going to get a proposal to

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:29.320
do something that might actually do something
about what's going on?

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:35.220
And the the biggest problem, arguably in the
United States is gun culture.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:42.000
And it's the idea of seeing firearms as something
to bolster masculinity, something to make

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.150
political points, something to solve interpersonal
problems.

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:52.050
And of course, if we resolved that, there
would be way fewer other problems to figure

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:53.050
out.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:54.050
Now, that's not the case.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:55.289
The situation is far more complicated than
that.

00:00:55.289 --> 00:00:58.870
And so as a result, we need to do other things.

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:03.510
I'm really glad to say, even though who the
hell knows if this has any shot of becoming

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:05.009
a reality?

00:01:05.009 --> 00:01:10.490
About two weeks after that incident in which
the gunman shot nine coworkers at the San

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:17.209
Jose light rail yard, CNN is reporting that
the mayor of San Jose is proposing something

00:01:17.209 --> 00:01:19.310
that I've talked about before.

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:23.490
Other gun safety advocates have talked about
before, but has not really been taken very

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:29.740
seriously anywhere, which is a restriction
that would require gun owners in the city

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:33.110
of San Jose to obtain insurance for their
firearm.

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:38.079
If they are a firearm owner, you must get
insurance, sort of like you do with a vehicle,

00:01:38.079 --> 00:01:45.689
the vehicle, although it's primarily for transportation,
you can do really irresponsible and dangerous,

00:01:45.689 --> 00:01:47.729
dangerous things with the vehicle.

00:01:47.729 --> 00:01:48.859
Things can also happen to the vehicle.

00:01:48.859 --> 00:01:53.929
And so in most states, you're required to
have insurance on the vehicle, much the same

00:01:53.929 --> 00:02:00.509
way you could require gun owners to have insurance
because they are gun owners as well as the

00:02:00.509 --> 00:02:04.549
proposal is to pay an annual fee to cover
the cost of gun violence.

00:02:04.549 --> 00:02:12.090
And this is one of those things that it you
know, most of the discussion is about let's

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:14.689
ban this type of gun, let's ban that type
of gun.

00:02:14.689 --> 00:02:17.840
That's something that we should be looking
into.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:19.410
Universal background checks.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:20.410
Absolutely.

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:26.430
But treating firearms the way we treat vehicles,
which includes licensing requirements and

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:32.430
relicensing requirements, as well as mandatory
insurance in both in most states, is actually

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:33.590
a really good idea.

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:37.440
Now, the mayor of San Jose is Sam Licadho
or Licadho.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:39.510
I'm not sure how it's pronounced.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:44.120
He unveiled this earlier this week and he
said, quote, If we cannot stop the horrors

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:48.599
of gun violence in our cities and this is
important because just requiring insurance

00:02:48.599 --> 00:02:50.750
won't actually stop gun violence.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:55.549
But he says if we cannot stop the horrors
of gun violence in our cities, at least we're

00:02:55.549 --> 00:02:57.640
going to have the public stopped paying for
it.

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:02.209
The Second Amendment protects the right of
Americans to own guns, but does not require

00:03:02.209 --> 00:03:05.360
that every other taxpayer pay for that right.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:10.230
Requiring use gun users to pay fees will help
fund critical emergency medical and police

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:13.310
response and reduce our taxpayers burden.

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:18.999
The way the proposal would work, according
to CNN, is all gun and ammunition purchases

00:03:18.999 --> 00:03:24.370
would have to be recorded on video and audio
to discourage straw purchases, where people

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:30.939
who are legally ineligible to buy guns figure
out a way to get a gun through a straw purchaser.

00:03:30.939 --> 00:03:35.879
The straw purchasers would be far less willing
to do that if they knew that every transaction

00:03:35.879 --> 00:03:40.959
that was legal at some point it's a legal
gun, that they would be less likely to do

00:03:40.959 --> 00:03:41.959
that.

00:03:41.959 --> 00:03:45.530
Additionally, suicide prevention materials
would be required at point of sale.

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:50.170
This is taking seriously something that many
gun rights advocates point out, which is,

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:52.569
hey, a lot of these deaths are suicide.

00:03:52.569 --> 00:03:53.569
OK, yeah.

00:03:53.569 --> 00:03:57.579
So we basically have three categories of problems
with gun violence.

00:03:57.579 --> 00:03:59.209
We have suicides.

00:03:59.209 --> 00:04:04.019
There's no reason not to admit that that's
an issue that is dealt with very differently

00:04:04.019 --> 00:04:07.829
than individual handgun homicides.

00:04:07.829 --> 00:04:12.110
You will often hear the rights say, you know,
all this focus on AR 15s, most of the deaths

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:13.110
are coming from handguns.

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:15.620
Well, we need an approach for handguns.

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:18.079
And then you have the mass shootings.

00:04:18.079 --> 00:04:24.160
These are three different problems, all under
the umbrella of gun violence and gun death.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:27.250
And we need different approaches for each
of them.

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:33.860
Lakatos or Lakatos proposal also includes
leveraging federal information for early intervention.

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:37.750
This is something that's relevant because
we often will hear and in the case of San

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:44.490
Jose, it was the case that the gunman had
had a previous interaction with law enforcement.

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:49.530
He had been detained by Customs and Border
Protection officers who discovered books on

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:54.330
terrorism and writings that were filled with
hatred towards his workplace.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:56.230
He ended up shooting up his workplace.

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:59.450
A San Jose police were never notified.

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:04.699
And had no idea that this is someone that
should have been on their radar and there's

00:05:04.699 --> 00:05:08.930
a lot of good meat to this proposal now, the
gun rights people, of course, are going to

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:10.550
be against it.

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:12.960
However, not all of them are against it.

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:17.860
And I've said this before, you know, it's
not just Republicans who own the guns.

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:21.760
Yes, it's it's probably more than 50 percent.

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:27.020
But I know many people on the left who also
own guns and every single one of them, particularly

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:34.139
in blue states, is fine with all of this stuff
because they realize that it makes sense for

00:05:34.139 --> 00:05:37.900
there to be some hurdles to clear to obtain
firearms.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:44.260
If you think driving comes with significant
responsibility and licensing makes sense and

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:49.449
insurance makes sense and relicensing and
registration fees and all of these different

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:55.300
filters make sense as as my liberal friends
tend to believe, then it follows that the

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:58.100
same would be a requirement of something like
firearms.

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:02.380
You're not restricting the Second Amendment
by putting these restrictions in place.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:07.919
You are not limiting one's ability to obtain
a firearm if as long as they are willing to

00:06:07.919 --> 00:06:09.110
go through these processes.

00:06:09.110 --> 00:06:12.039
So I have no idea if this will go anywhere
in San Jose.

00:06:12.039 --> 00:06:18.289
I have no idea if there would be problems
from from higher courts on legal challenge.

00:06:18.289 --> 00:06:20.250
This is just step one.

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:23.909
But I've been talking about mandatory gun
insurance for years at this point on this

00:06:23.909 --> 00:06:28.250
program, and I'm really happy to see that
this is actually being proposed.

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:29.759
Let me know what else you think.

00:06:29.759 --> 00:06:31.050
Oh, and let me mention it.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:37.379
Speaking of what else, changing culture around
using firearms in the United States, there

00:06:37.379 --> 00:06:41.509
are examples of countries with lots of firearms
that don't have our problems.

00:06:41.509 --> 00:06:45.389
And the difference is the people, the we have
a problem with the people in this country

00:06:45.389 --> 00:06:49.099
seeing firearms as a way to solve problems.

00:06:49.099 --> 00:06:53.729
And listen, universal health care, there's
no doubt that if you really want to take seriously,

00:06:53.729 --> 00:06:57.360
you know, if you're a gun rights activist
and you want to take even if you're cynical

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:03.330
in your desire to take attention off of mass
shootings and and homicides by putting the

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:09.349
focus on suicides, if you want to be serious
about that, then support universal health

00:07:09.349 --> 00:07:15.639
care of some kind, whether it's Medicare for
all, whether it's some kind of provision for

00:07:15.639 --> 00:07:22.530
mental health care that is always available
regardless of insurance status.

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:28.599
Because if you really want to deal with suicides
and by the way, mass shootings and individual

00:07:28.599 --> 00:07:33.490
handgun homicides, how are we not giving people
full access to mental health care?

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:37.070
So if you want to really put your money where
your mouth is, as someone who claims to if

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:41.879
you're on the right and say the real problem
is suicides, what is your plan for getting

00:07:41.879 --> 00:07:47.939
health care to everybody so that everybody
has access to to a therapist and to whatever

00:07:47.939 --> 00:07:49.870
it is that they need along that front?

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:54.580
But my question to you is, let me know what
else you believe is the lowest hanging fruit

00:07:54.580 --> 00:08:20.919
as far as firearms 

00:08:20.919 --> 00:09:02.560
are concerned.

